============================================================================
E. THE BINDING FRACTION tau* = phi^-2 IS UNIVERSAL IN THE ALPHABET SIZE
============================================================================
  Replacing 2^(t-i) by b^(t-i) leaves the identity (K) and hence the
  reduction (V) <=> (1-tau)^2 = tau untouched; only (T) moves, giving
  u*(b) = phi/(b+phi) and gamma*(b) = log(phi)/log((b+phi)/phi).

     b    gamma* numeric   log(phi)/log((b+phi)/phi)   worst tau   phi^-2
     2    0.597987433      0.597987436            0.382000   0.381966
     3    0.458840046      0.458840048            0.382000   0.381966
     4    0.386586952      0.386586954            0.382000   0.381966
  b=2 is special ONLY because (2+phi)/phi = sqrt 5 exactly
     (2+phi)/phi = 2.236067977500   sqrt 5 = 2.236067977500
  VERDICT E: tau* universal, gamma*(b) formula holds: True

